1. Parent Class
class ParentClass {
    void methodName() {
        // parent method
    }
}

2. Child Class
class ChildClass extends ParentClass {
    void methodName() {
        // child method
    }
}

3. Main Class
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) 
    {
        ParentClass obj = new ChildClass();
        obj.methodName();
    }
}

Most Important Syntax :
ParentClass obj = new ChildClass();
| Part               | Meaning        |
| ------------------ | -------------- |
| `ParentClass`      | Reference type |
| `obj`              | Object name    |
| `new ChildClass()` | Child object   |

Code Flow :
1. Create Parent class
2. Create Child class using extends
3. Override same method
4. Create parent reference + child object
5. Call method
